The [[Sootopolis Gym]] specializes in {{type|Water}} Pokémon. Water-type moves are super effective against {{t|Fire}}-, {{t|Ground}}-, and {{type|Rock}} Pokémon, while Water-type Pokémon are weak to {{t|Electric}}- and {{type|Grass}} moves.

The Gym features two levels. The upper level is filled with ice tiles; stepping on them once cracks them. Stepping on them a second time shatters them, leaving a challenger to fall to the snowy area below where several Gym Trainers await. There are three sections of icy floor; each icy tile must be passed over in order to clear the current puzzle and reveal the stairway to the next area.
* Area 1: Move northeast, then northwest in a simple "S" shape (→1, ↑1, ←2, ↑1, ↑1).
* Area 2: Go toward the northwest corner first, then to the southeast corner (←3, ↑2, →2, ↓1, →3, ↓1, →1). Move northwest from here (↑2, ←3) to clear the puzzle.
* Area 3: Move to the southeast corner first (→2, ↑1, →2, ↓1, →1), then to the northeast corner (↑3). Zigzag westward for a short distance (←2, ↓1, ←1, ↑1, ←1), then southwest (↓2, ←2, ↓1) to pass by the stairway from Area 2. Zigzag westward again (←1, ↑1, ←1, ↓1, ←1, ↑1, ←1) to the wall, then move to the northwest corner (↑2). Zigzag eastward this time (→1, ↓1, →1, ↑1, →1, ↓1, →1, ↑1, →1) to reveal the final stairway to the [[Gym Leader]].

[[Wallace]] leads with his {{p|Luvdisc}}; a {{stat|Speed|speedy}} Pokémon, but its offenses are lacking. However, it can still trigger {{status|confusion}} with {{m|Sweet Kiss}}, and further hinder any opposite-gender opponents with {{m|Attract}}. As a {{2t|Water|Ground}} Pokémon, his {{p|Whiscash}} takes massive damage from {{type|Grass}} attacks, but is immune to {{t|Electric}} moves. {{m|Rain Dance}} temporarily boosts the power of {{type|Water}} attacks, and {{m|Earthquake}} helps deter Electric-type opponents. Most of {{p|Sealeo}}'s moves deal damage, but {{m|Encore}} locks the target into using its previous move again. Its {{2t|Water|Ice}} typing gives it additional weaknesses to {{t|Fighting}} and {{t|Rock}} moves. His {{p|Seaking}} is better suited to [[physical move]]s, but {{m|Fury Attack}} is not very strong. However, using Rain Dance has a two-pronged effect: Its {{a|Swift Swim}} Ability doubles its Speed during [[rain]], and powers up its {{m|Water Pulse}} attack. Lower-leveled Pokémon should beware of its {{m|Horn Drill}}! Finally, his {{p|Milotic}} can deal a good deal of damage with Water Pulse and fight back against Grass Pokémon with {{m|Ice Beam}}. High {{stat|Special Defense}} means that physical moves are more useful, but avoid causing status ailments: its {{a|Marvel Scale}} Ability gives it a 50% {{stat|Defense}} boost when suffering!

